WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.130
On the eighth of November, at least five
hundred and thirty-one million dollars

2
00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.700
of positions were liquidated
in fifteen minutes.

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.066
In moments like that, one question
decides what your token holders get:

4
00:00:12.066 --> 00:00:13.918
was the liquidity actually there?

5
00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:18.008
Token teams pay market makers
to keep order books deep.

6
00:00:18.388 --> 00:00:19.814
But most teams cannot check.

7
00:00:20.194 --> 00:00:22.054
Price sites show a snapshot of right now.

8
00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:25.788
Market-maker dashboards show
what the market maker reports.

9
00:00:26.168 --> 00:00:30.329
What is missing is an independent record
of what every book actually held —

10
00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:33.492
every five minutes — including
the minutes that mattered.

11
00:00:34.542 --> 00:00:37.899
WATAM Intelligence reads every
order book of your token,

12
00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:41.915
on each of the twenty-three exchanges
we cover, at the same moment,

13
00:00:41.915 --> 00:00:44.492
every five minutes —
and keeps the history.

14
00:00:44.872 --> 00:00:47.147
Underneath, we read
your on-chain DEX pools.

15
00:00:47.527 --> 00:00:51.934
Beside them, perpetual futures: open
interest, funding and liquidations.

16
00:00:52.314 --> 00:00:56.122
We count a trading pair only after
verifying it really is your token.

17
00:00:56.502 --> 00:01:01.627
And we quote what a real sell would receive,
through 1inch, 0x, KyberSwap and Velora.

18
00:01:02.007 --> 00:01:06.238
Independent. No data from your market
maker. Nothing you have to integrate.

19
00:01:07.288 --> 00:01:09.761
Here is what we recorded
at five to ten that night.

20
00:01:10.141 --> 00:01:13.288
Across fifty-two mid-cap
tokens, bids within two percent

21
00:01:13.288 --> 00:01:15.479
of the price fell thirty-eight percent.

22
00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:17.781
Eleven tokens lost more than half.

23
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.017
Same tokens, same five minutes:

24
00:01:20.017 --> 00:01:23.791
on one exchange the books kept
forty-one percent of their bids.

25
00:01:24.171 --> 00:01:25.259
On another, eighty-eight.

26
00:01:25.639 --> 00:01:28.684
And the on-chain pools?
Ninety-six percent still there.

27
00:01:29.064 --> 00:01:31.258
That difference is
invisible in a snapshot.

28
00:01:31.638 --> 00:01:33.346
It is exactly what you are paying for.

29
00:01:34.396 --> 00:01:37.448
The Market Maker Scorecard
turns this into one page

30
00:01:37.448 --> 00:01:41.636
you can share with your community,
your exchange or your market maker:

31
00:01:41.636 --> 00:01:45.645
hour by hour, exchange by exchange,
did the depth you pay for hold?

32
00:01:46.025 --> 00:01:48.434
Live Pro watches it for you and alerts you

33
00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:52.392
the moment it stops holding —
including during a liquidation cascade.

34
00:01:53.442 --> 00:01:56.957
The Market Maker Scorecard is four
hundred and ninety dollars a month.

35
00:01:57.337 --> 00:02:01.123
Until the thirtieth of November,
our first teams can run a thirty-day

36
00:02:01.123 --> 00:02:04.031
founder pilot for one hundred
and forty-nine dollars.

37
00:02:04.411 --> 00:02:08.019
Live Pro alerts start at four hundred
and ninety-nine dollars a month.

38
00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:13.137
Exchanges and market makers can license
the data across every token we track.

39
00:02:14.187 --> 00:02:18.977
Our vision is simple: liquidity you can
verify, not liquidity you are told about.

40
00:02:19.357 --> 00:02:20.333
Send us your token.

41
00:02:20.713 --> 00:02:22.482
We will show you what
your books really held.
